{"event_id":"kimi-final:3","seq":3,"run_id":"kimi-final","session_id":"kimi-final","created_at":1789612749.432,"terminal":true,"type":"done","payload":{"status":"completed","last_seq":2,"result_summary":"approved: 2 finding(s)","review":{"schema_version":1,"verdict":"approved","risk":"read_only","markdown":"# Review\n\nAll five criteria pass on the supplied bounded evidence. Binding: host-constructed identity (scope/run/generation/effectKey/invocation/candidate/artifact/command/image) is hashed into bindingRef, persisted before create, folded into specDigest, and re-verified against launch, container inspect, and stop receipts; the substitution test confirms cross-candidate/image/generation/invocation/container tampering is rejected. Isolation: build executes only host FROM/COPY/WORKDIR with candidate bytes as inert data, pull=false, network=none, base and built images inspected for ONBUILD/volumes; runtime has no mounts, network none, readonly rootfs, cap-drop ALL, non-root, and full config re-inspection before start. Settlement: exit codes are read only after verified physical removal (204+404+durable receipt); valid fail codes settle confirmed passed=false, unregistered codes/cancellation become non-retryable trusted failures, lost DELETE ACK yields unknown with admission retained and replay sealed. Join: latest-ledger recomputation with digest-pinned race check routes pass/fail/unknown correctly and preserves the shell command path. Journal: atomic no-replace durable writes ordered binding->create->launch->start->stop receipt; confirmStopped fails closed. No blocking findings.","judgments":[{"id":"binding","pass":true,"severity":"warning","summary":"Candidate bytes, pinned image, ledger effect, generation, invocation and container ID are linked via host-computed bindingRef/specDigest and receipt chains; worker/model identity is never an input; substitution tests reject tampering."},{"id":"isolation","pass":true,"severity":"warning","summary":"Image preparation runs only host-generated FROM/COPY/WORKDIR with candidate files as data, no pull/network, base+built image ONBUILD/volume inspection; execution keeps network none, no mounts, readonly rootfs, dropped caps, non-root user and verified container config."},{"id":"settlement","pass":true,"severity":"warning","summary":"Business pass/fail is derived from exit codes only after verified physical stop; registered fail codes give confirmed passed=false; ambiguity (lost DELETE ACK) retains admission and seals replay; synchronous authorization is rechecked throughout."},{"id":"join","pass":true,"severity":"warning","summary":"Join recomputes from the latest ledger with binding/artifact/evidence validation and snapshot race detection; normal and allowlisted-nonzero exits reach complete join/repair/stop decisions; contained and shell paths both supported."},{"id":"journal","pass":true,"severity":"warning","summary":"Exact identity is durably written (atomic no-replace link + fsync) before create, launch before start, stop receipt after confirmed removal; lost stop acknowledgement never authorizes release or replay."}],"findings":[{"rule_id":"contained.trusted-daemon-tamper-window","severity":"info","message":"Base-image safety inspection and build are separate daemon calls, so a retag between them is only detectable via the trusted daemon; this is explicitly inside the stated trust boundary (daemon/base image trusted) and out of scope.","file":"packages/agents/src/contained-image.ts","fingerprint":"978b4b030fc64e40030020324d65821f3911fa57fb646bc56fac1b8fb49ae388"},{"rule_id":"contained.output-bounded","severity":"info","message":"Container output is bounded (tail=100 frames, 16KiB slice) and evidence store marks previews as lossy with full-stream hash/length; acceptable per documented diagnostic-only capture semantics.","file":"packages/agents/src/contained-command.ts","fingerprint":"43c4a0ea1ff0edc58272ae2aff984edcad39c20e193665a92ff8410373b0ce93"}],"recommended_actions":[],"evid